WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.674
Week 16: Weather, Nature, and Plans. understand a forecast describe terrain change plans because of conditions

2
00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:20.876
Operational objective. By the end of this section you can understand a forecast, describe terrain, change plans because of conditions. The focus is useful performance, not isolated terminology.

3
00:00:20.876 --> 00:00:28.934
Language system. Weather expressions; present progressive; impersonal se; conditional planning with si + present.

4
00:00:28.934 --> 00:00:34.987
Sound and delivery. Chunk long noun phrases and retain clear sentence focus.

5
00:00:34.987 --> 00:00:44.519
Core principle. Notice meaning first, then form. Retrieve the new language aloud, compare it with the model, and repair one feature at a time.

6
00:00:44.519 --> 00:01:12.527
Model language. Mañana va a llover en la costa. — It is going to rain on the coast tomorrow. Hace viento en las zonas altas. — It is windy in the highlands. Si cambia el tiempo, regresamos temprano. — If the weather changes, we will return early. Se prohíbe encender fuego en el bosque. — Lighting fires in the forest is prohibited. Estamos protegiendo una fuente de agua. — We are protecting a water source.

7
00:01:12.527 --> 00:01:22.531
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
